      "title": "Funnel Analyzer: Troubleshooting Configuration Drift and Propagation Errors",
      "content_summary": "Guidance for resolving issues where configuration changes in Funnel Analyzer fail to take effect, resulting in data mismatches or unresponsive services due to environment variable errors or template misconfigurations.",
      "content_body": "When users report that feature flags are not applying or data appears inconsistent, first verify that the latest configuration template has been successfully propagated to all active instances. Check the internal environment variables to ensure no values are missing or overridden by local settings, as this often causes silent configuration failures. If the issue persists, audit the current policy settings against the supported configuration schema, as outdated documentation may lead customers to apply unsupported parameters. Typically, resolving these drift issues requires a manual configuration change or a policy correction, followed by educating the customer on the updated best practices."
